I've fixed the prepare order so the product worktrees exist before the project's `specdojo build` runs. I haven't run the new integration tests or the type check myself; the parent runner runs those (`test-integration`, `typecheck` and the other checks) after I exit.

**The fix (`src/exec-worktree-ops.ts`)**
- When `project/` is created, `checkpointAndEnsureWorktree` now holds back the build step. It creates the product worktrees (`ensureProductWorktrees`) first, then runs the build (`generateWorktreeArtifacts`), then makes the checkpoint commit. Hooks that read the config at commit time also see the product directories this way.
- When an existing `project/` worktree is reused, the product worktrees are created or reused before the build too. A re-run now recovers from an earlier prepare that stopped before the product worktrees were made, which is how this bug left things.
- Projects without `repos` behave as before, apart from the build now running just after setup instead of inside it.

**Tests added (`tests/src/exec-task-repos.integration.test.ts`)**
- A stand-in for `specdojo build` (`dist/specdojo.js`) that fails if `../app1` or `../app2` is missing, the way the config loader does. The test checks that prepare reaches the checkpoint commit and the build runs exactly once.
- A test that deletes the product worktrees and re-runs prepare. It checks that both are recreated (`created: true`) while `project/` is reused.

**Ticket (`pjr-nn43-...md`)**: I filled in the 「対応結果」 section (fix, what was checked, prevention). I didn't change the status fields or the index.

**Checks I ran**
- `npx prettier --write` on all three changed files.
- `register build` and `catalog validate` (both `--project prj-0001`) passed. The catalog check printed only existing `based_on` warnings.
- `npm run -s validate:history-links` passed; the changed ticket is `valid`.

